1
00:00:00,520 --> 00:00:03,560
Five thousand years ago, ink was memory you could carry.

2
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:09,600
In China, scribes ground lamp-black with glue into sticks ink that out-lasted kings.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:14,020
Around 1440, Gutenberg split the word into movable type.

4
00:00:14,240 --> 00:00:18,520
And in 1455, the Gutenberg Bible poured from the press.

5
00:00:18,980 --> 00:00:22,440
Everything you have ever read began as a stubborn black promise.

6
00:00:22,760 --> 00:00:24,680
This is ink. It remembers.
